+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5930+) **GitHub workflow build checks:** added GitHub Actions checks under [`.github/workflows`](/.github/workflows/) to catch forgotten debug/default settings and data drift at each commit. Current checks notably verify launch-guard sentinel values, XML tag references in SAS define text values, integer SAS define bounds, valid main-menu opening-music script setup, disabled BBAI logging defaults, shared UI font defaults, Sevopedia Leader AI Personality Panel predumped-cache defaults and predump file presence, `SAS_MAGIC_WORLDSIZE_*` constants matching `CIV4WorldInfo.xml` order, and every playable `PrivateMaps/*.py` being listed exactly once across the SAS map-script heaviness/coverage defines while every listed map script exists in `PrivateMaps/`. For example, this helped spot [map scripts that were previously unclassified in SAS map-script heaviness defines](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27198308080/job/80295526028); they are now listed explicitly for exhaustiveness (more robust; no gameplay change). The checks also run locally with Python 3; see [`.github/workflows/README.md`](/.github/workflows/README.md).
 - **Handicap XML comparison helper:** added [`compare_handicap_infos.py`](/LLM_Helpers/compare_handicap_infos.py), a report-only, mod-agnostic helper that compares two explicit `CIV4HandicapInfo.xml` file paths, inside or outside this mod folder, by handicap index; shows missing fields as blanks, includes absolute/percentage numeric deltas, and embeds a spreadsheet-friendly TSV matrix. The shipped stable example [`handicap_infos_compared.md`](/LLM_Helpers/examples/handicap_infos_compared.md) compares base AdvCiv 1.12 vs AdvCiv-SAS. See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).
 - **Merged** the **old split/interdependent Foreign Advisor** implementation from the two-file setup (`CvForeignAdvisor.py` + `CvExoticForeignAdvisor.py`) into a **single unified** [CvForeignAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvForeignAdvisor.py) with the **full tab set** (as of now Relations/Glance/Active/Bonus/Info/Tech/Cities). In our findings, **this was the only screen file** using that **interdependent split** pattern, so merging it into one file directly **fixes that inconsistency** and **reduces maintenance burden**; other major screen files such as [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py) and [CvInfoScreen.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvInfoScreen.py) are lengthy but unified files. By contrast, true alternatives use independent variants (for example BUG/non-BUG [CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvBUGMilitaryAdvisor.py) / [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py) paths), not interdependent split files.
 - **Remove screen-dependent geometry computation** from `__init__` in advisors because this advisor object is created before a reliable screen context exists; doing layout in `interfaceScreen` **ensures correct values for the current resolution**. Keeping **only screen-independent edge constants** in `__init__` ensures **no redundant recomputation** is made again in `interfaceScreen`, and **catches loud screen-dependent errors** in `__init__`.

